{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/121382-concept-critique-security-expert-psychopomp","id":121382,"title":"Concept Critique: Security Expert Psychopomp?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T19:32:59-07:00","id":121382,"title":"Concept Critique: Security Expert Psychopomp?","content":"Okay so when I've finished a formal write-up for the character I'm gonna post it here, but in the meantime I wanted to discuss the basics and get some thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> So they're a Psychopomp that was created as an expert security consultant for businesses in Seattle. His job was to create sophisticated security systems at those businesses the God-Machine needed modified in order to create back doors and weaknesses in the systems. His back doors and security serve a variety of effects, from enabling particular groups to access information (and misinformation) they shouldn't have, to getting a certain hacker caught and jailed so he could be murdered in the prison yard at exactly 26:00 in the afternoon, etcetera.<br /> <br /> I haven't nailed down if it's part of a particular project or if he just serves a more general purpose, I'm wondering if you guys think one or the other would be more compelling? I'm also trying to unpack what being a &quot;security consultant&quot; should mean. I'm thinking he designs both physical security systems as well as doing the computer stuff. Does that make sense? Is it a bit too TV profession-like? Do you think it'd be an acceptable concession to have his job be that?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why he fell, but I'm thinking it has something to do with him being dissatisfied with the God-Machine requiring him to build systems with artificial weaknesses. He's a perfectionist by nature, and he wants his works to be flawless. He doesn't understand the need for the flaws, any more than he might understand the plans behind their being exploited. That lack of communication was upsetting and frustrating, until eventually he disobeyed the order and made it flawless to see what would happen if he did. At that point, he probably fell.<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking he's an Inquisitor, and the Embed I've currently got picked for him as his First Key is Download Knowledge. My ST likes it as a first pick, and I just want to see what you guys think. Thematically, the idea I have is that his think is about exponential self-improvement. He's obsessed with executing things with maximum efficiency and doing them as perfectly as possible. Abstractly, I think he things figuring out how to improve himself is how he can learn to understand the God-Machine and achieve Hell. Though he's probably not thought about it that way exactly.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think of that justification, or the schtick of being a Demonic perfectionist? Do you think that jives with what else I've explained about his background? What about with his Fall?<br /> <br /> One of the other merits I've been looking at has been the merit &quot;Alternate Identity&quot; Here, I was looking at the part of Inquisitors which discusses how paranoid they are, and I'm thinking of ways to incorporate that into a guy who does security stuff for a living. I figure he knows a lot of tricks that people might use to falsify their identities, and is probably pretty good at it himself. After his fall, he might've set up an alternate identity which comes with a disguise, which he might use to meet his Demonic compatriots.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think that's good, or does it sound a bit dumb? I'm trying to figure out how to slot his paranoia and desire to remain &quot;hidden&quot; with the perfectionist in him and his desire for self improvement. I don't think they necessarily conflict, but I'm having a hard time wrapping them up with a bow.<br /> <br /> Any other thoughts you guys might have would be appreciated. Does all of this sound like a fun Demon to interact with? Do you have any other questions you think I should be asking myself? Should I post a truncated character sheet?<br /> <br /> Any help is appreciated. I feel like my character game hasn't been on point recently, and I want to tighten it up.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-29-2014, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T16:55:33-07:00","id":122775,"title":"","content":"Been able to get a little discussion on this going in another Board, curious if it'll give anyone anything to think about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?724462-Demon-The-Descent-Concept-Critique-Security-Expert-Psychopomp\" target=\"_blank\">rpg.net</a><br /> <br /> How do you guys view Cover? This conversation has me questioning my interpretation, which is that knowledge of the Cover Falls with you, hence why the God-Machine doesn't just pick you up again. Does that sound right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T20:08:49-07:00","id":123585,"title":"","content":"I posted his character sheet on rpg.net in summary format, guess it wouldn't hurt to pop that up here, too. Let me know what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryptonym, the Security Singularity</b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Methodical</span></span><br /> <b>Vice:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Curious</span></span><br /> <b>Incarnation:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Psychopomp</span></span><br /> <b>Agenda:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Inquisitor</span></span><br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 2</span></span><br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 1</span></span><br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Academics 2, *Computer (Hacking) 4, Crafts 2, Investigation 2, Science (Chemistry) 1</span></span><br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Athletics 1, Firearms 2, *Larceny (Infiltration, Security Systems) 3, Stealth 1</span></span><br /> <b>Social Skills:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Persuasion 1, *Subterfuge (Disguise, Lies) 3 </span></span><br /> <b>Merits:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Professional Training (Security Expert) 4, Contacts (Corporate Sector, Hackers) 2, Alternate Identity 3, Resources (Upper Middle Class) 3</span></span><br /> <b>Health:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 6</span></span><br /> <b>Primum:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1</span></span><br /> <b>Demonic Form: </b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Rivet Arm, Electrical Sight, Inhuman Intelligence, Clairvoyant Sight, Mirrored Skin, Phasing, Memory Theft</span></span><br /> <b>Embeds:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Download Knowledge (First Key), Raw Materials, Alibi</span></span><br /> <b>Exploits:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Deep Pockets</span></span><br /> <b>Aether/per turn:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 10/1</span></span><br /> <b>Willpower:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 5</span></span><br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Fill out his Cover's Life (long), Investigate the Ring, Find local Infrastructure</span></span><br /> <b>Cover:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 7</span></span><br /> <b>Size:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 5</span></span><br /> <b>Speed:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 10</span></span><br /> <b>Defense:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 4</span></span><br /> <b>Initiative:</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 6</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>*Asset Skills (Security Expert): </b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Computer, Larceny, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think of the name? If you're wondering, yes, I'm fully aware of what it means. :P</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-01-2014, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T06:27:43-07:00","id":123744,"title":"","content":"Not to be mean or anything: the character looks fine. Just.... boring.<br /> <br /> As for the name, I'd go with something simplier, that only hints at what he does rather than coming right out and screaming it. What's his cover? A Kevin Mitnick wannabe? A balding white dude who looks like he goes home and eats TV dinners for fun? Perhaps a high strung woman who wears her hair in the tightest bun you've ever seen? Ms. Grey, or Mr. Screen might work. Remember though that last names are typically words that are older than the internet, so you'll want to use words that have been around longer but are still used in computer lingo. Mr. Hack maybe? Web? Key?<br /> <br /> Second, I barely see anything on the sheet that hints at the fall, which was a life changing event after all. Why did he fall? You mentioned that perhaps its his perfectionist nature. Perhaps before his fall, the angel became obsessed with some other hobby that further aggravated it, like gardening or painting? I believe the book reccomends you have one skill that is cover threatening - pick something that would seem out of place for an angel with your job to know, and give demon you some depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T07:14:54-07:00","id":123763,"title":"","content":"That's fair. Do you think his position is too conventional? The elements of his personality are too typical or archetypal for a Demon? What are the parts that make it seem boring?<br /> <br /> I'll admit I think the thing I'm most interested in doing is playing a character who has a technology background, but I can readily see how that might be a bit too boring for a Demon. That said, if it gets me a more interesting character, I'm comfortable revising that.<br /> <br /> I've made a few Demons before but I haven't done a great job making more unconventional concepts, and I fear I haven't really taken to heart the suggestions they have for concepts. A more apt description of Cryptonym might be &quot;Paranoid Security Expert&quot; and that's hardly as incongruous as the Fire-and-brimstone Buddhist Preacher, for instance.<br /> <br /> I think I may have chosen Chemistry as my cover-violating Specialty, but that seems hardly evocative, so that among other things will probably need to go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-02-2014, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:44:47-07:00","id":124156,"title":"","content":"Since I'm suspecting the concept's boring nature is at least in part due to the cover being some kind of security guy, do you guys have any suggestions for something that might be more intriguing?<br /> <br /> Can anything be salvaged here, or should I be going back to the drawing board?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:20:15-07:00","id":124180,"title":"","content":"Computer IT would give him a cute &quot;boring&quot; day job, repairing desktops at offices. That'd give him access to install programs on those unwitting victims, would keep his skillset useful, and serve as an excellent tie in for plot hooks relating to mundane job vs demonic job. For his Fall, perhaps God utilized one of his backdoor programs (one of his masterpieces) to collapse the security system itself. Angry and bitter at God for betraying him and his work, and deciding his perfect talents would serve him better elsewhere.. he left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:55:13-07:00","id":124206,"title":"","content":"That's actually a pretty good idea, maybe he's tech support at the Ayers Risk Control company? Or are you thinking one of the types that travels to other businesses to fix their tech woes?<br /> <br /> His cover is an unremarkable looking dude in his mid-30s. Head shaven, glasses, he looks like the kind of guy who should be in a management position, which might seem particularly incongruous if he isn't.<br /> <br /> Another thought I had is someone who works in construction, not as a worker, but as management.<br /> <br /> Another thought might be he's a building safety inspector. My problem with these two is that while they're cool covers, they wouldn't really lend themselves to the skillset I'd like to play with. Being an IT guy honestly seems best to me.<br /> <br /> Also revised his name right now to Mr. Wire. I'm thinking it's a nice play on dealing with eletronics and stuff like wiretapping and surveillance. Does that sound cool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-02-2014, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T23:30:02-07:00","id":124313,"title":"","content":"Okay, so revision.<br /> <br /> He's themed around infiltrating something and then arranging something else to happen. Revising the particulars because I'm unhappy with what I currently have.<br /> <br /> Is that appropriate for a Psychopomp, or would that be the purview of another Incarnation?<br /> <br /> Currently I the (admittedly lame) idea I'm working through is that he was supposed to install surveillance for an organization he'd infiltrated in certain key areas in the city as part of an occult matrix. Then the surveillance stuff would detect a specific individual at all the locations, then kill them at the last one in a mass of confusion. The mysterious individual disappears, the strike team sent to kill him disappears.<br /> <br /> The output of the Matrix is Concealment Infrastructure which blankets the area in-between the surveillance sites that Mr. Wire set up. This Concealment Infrastructure means that through unfortunate circumstances or the inadequacy of the people in charge, any attempts to surveil the area (and unwittingly stumble upon the infrastructure contained within it) are distracted or otherwise rendered ineffective.<br /> <br /> So that's what I'm working with. Not super happy. The burning question remains: Is this appropriate for a Psychopomp?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T07:45:23-07:00","id":124482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/121382-concept-critique-security-expert-psychopomp?p=124313#post124313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so revision.<br /> <br /> He's themed around infiltrating something and then arranging something else to happen. Revising the particulars because I'm unhappy with what I currently have.<br /> <br /> Is that appropriate for a Psychopomp, or would that be the purview of another Incarnation?<br /> <br /> Currently I the (admittedly lame) idea I'm working through is that he was supposed to install surveillance for an organization he'd infiltrated in certain key areas in the city as part of an occult matrix. Then the surveillance stuff would detect a specific individual at all the locations, then kill them at the last one in a mass of confusion. The mysterious individual disappears, the strike team sent to kill him disappears.<br /> <br /> The output of the Matrix is Concealment Infrastructure which blankets the area in-between the surveillance sites that Mr. Wire set up. This Concealment Infrastructure means that through unfortunate circumstances or the inadequacy of the people in charge, any attempts to surveil the area (and unwittingly stumble upon the infrastructure contained within it) are distracted or otherwise rendered ineffective.<br /> <br /> So that's what I'm working with. Not super happy. The burning question remains: Is this appropriate for a Psychopomp?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wheel I'm currently working on, Miss Spoke, had a Cover as a graffiti artist. Regardless of what impact the occult symbols hidden in her work had on anyone who happened to see them, her job description amounted to &quot;manipulate the symbolism of these locations to arrange a series of occult matrices,&quot; which is why she's a Psychopomp and not a Trumpet.<br /> <br /> Here you've got a similar situation where Wire's job was setting up pieces of Infrastructure that happened to be designed to result in somebody dying.<br /> <br /> Seems appropriate enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T05:39:39-07:00","id":125740,"title":"","content":"First: technology background in general is good. In general it fits well into the setting, you just need to add a twist that isn't there already just because you're a demon.<br /> <br /> I think of the difference between angels and Demons is that the fall is the process of going from a 2 dimensional caricature of an intelligent being to becoming a 3 dimensional caricature of a person. You fall because you gain some depth of personality, start questioning your directives and think for yourself. Try to think about why your demon fell and what he would do with his new found freedom once he no longer has a god given mission that drives him 24/7.<br /> <br /> To be more direct: forget &quot;paranoid&quot; in your description - all demons are either paranoid or stupid and dead. It goes without saying. Think up some other descriptive words. If it helps, research some of the more interesting &quot;Security experts&quot; in both media and real life. I've mentioned Kevin Mitnick, there's also Neo (hint, famous white and black hat hackers are good) - some hackers are street smart, some are skilled social manipulators. Some quick suggestions off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> &quot;Gumshoe security expert&quot; - If you want, go corny and give him a 50s era fedora and rainslick, and a speciality for investigating blood splatters as his cover threatening skill. He's still a hacker/security expert, but a hacker who loves old detective movies.<br /> <br /> &quot;Puppetmaster security expert&quot; - Perhaps you wish to have a character who enjoys manipulating things behind the scenes and working through cats paws. Give him a cult and send them on missions a la deepvoice. Bonus points if your cover turns out to be a skinny, acne prone kid in dire need of a tan and some nasel spray.<br /> <br /> As a note though: these are suggestions to make your character more interesting. What you have so far is a good baseline: I'm just throwing out suggestions that might move it from 'Generic concept&quot; to &quot;Awesome character to play&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:28:21-07:00","id":125825,"title":"","content":"Doublepost because I apparently didn't see the more recent update:<br /> <br /> I like the name and his mission before the fall is fine. I wouldn't worry about it being 'lame' - it only seems lame because you know all the details. For a storyteller, the drama of the story is created by not having all the facts. In other words, it seems lame because of the style its presented in, not because its actually bad.<br /> <br /> At this point, you're just looking for a twist - some fodder your storyteller can use when determining your ciphers. This sounds like it's almost there:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He's themed around infiltrating something and then arranging something else to happen. </div> </div> </div>Expand on that. He gets in and then uses bureaucracy to slow things to a crawl? Or perhaps sabotage using traps (appropriate for his original mission) or maybe he's a specialist in taking an existing device or matrix and giving it additional abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}